; Every commodity with a price of its own is fetched in the batch call,
; grouped by the commodity of that price: AAPL in terms of EUR and EUR
; in terms of $.  EUR is not left out for also being the commodity AAPL
; is priced in, so -X $ values AAPL with both fresh quotes:
; 10 * 120 EUR * $1.20 = $1440.00 (the stale EUR rate gives $1320.00).

P 2024/01/01 EUR $1.10
P 2024/01/01 AAPL 100 EUR

2024/01/15 Opening balance
    Assets:Brokerage        10 AAPL
    Equity:Opening

test bal Assets:Brokerage -X $ --now 2030/06/15 --download --getquote $sourcepath/test/scripts/mock-getquote-batch-only.sh
            $1440.00  Assets:Brokerage
end test

test pricedb --now 2030/06/15 --download --getquote $sourcepath/test/scripts/mock-getquote-batch-only.sh
P 2024/01/01 00:00:00 AAPL EUR100
P 2024/06/15 00:00:00 AAPL EUR120
P 2024/01/01 00:00:00 EUR $1.10
P 2024/06/15 00:00:00 EUR $1.20
end test
